# POST /ipp/provision — step 2: WHO. A printer is granted to a principal,
# and a principal must exist before anything can be granted to it.
#
# Here it is a person: txco://user/create mints `user:usr_…` and binds the
# email to it, which is what makes the email a username. It is idempotent on
# the email — provisioning a second printer for the same address finds the
# same user (`created: false`). A product with its own nouns names its own
# principal instead (`pony:paris`) and binds the username with an account op.
WHEN ._prov.printer =~ /./ && ._prov.email =~ /./
  EXEC "txco://user/create"
    WITH email        = ._prov.email,
         display_name = ._prov.name,
         into         = "_user"
